      "document_hash": "b1cfde40c6ab6b5e9d7f255b3ccec68e4846fb248a0af4feaad062e25c5d717d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b1cfde40c6ab-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 10:02 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2012-11-184",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b1cfde40c6ab6b5e9d7f255b3ccec68e4846fb248a0af4feaad062e25c5d717d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b1cfde40c6ab-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: We'll hear argument first this morning in Case 11-184, Kloeckner v. Solis. Mr. Schnapper."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2012-11-184",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b1cfde40c6ab6b5e9d7f255b3ccec68e4846fb248a0af4feaad062e25c5d717d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b1cfde40c6ab-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Mr. Schnapper, could you clarify what the district court, as you see it, does? Does it deal only with the discrimination claim, or does it deal with the MSPB's procedural ruling?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2012-11-184",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b1cfde40c6ab6b5e9d7f255b3ccec68e4846fb248a0af4feaad062e25c5d717d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b1cfde40c6ab-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: But the critical point, I gather, is what standard of review the district court will apply to that exhaustion question, or the bar question, right?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2012-11-184",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "b1cfde40c6ab6b5e9d7f255b3ccec68e4846fb248a0af4feaad062e25c5d717d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b1cfde40c6ab-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Are you still standing by that distinction?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Schnapper",
      "case_id": "2012-11-184",
      "confidence": 0.94,
      "document_hash": "b1cfde40c6ab6b5e9d7f255b3ccec68e4846fb248a0af4feaad062e25c5d717d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b1cfde40c6ab-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Our view is that all mixed cases go to the district court."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Harrington",
      "case_id": "2012-11-184",
      "confidence": 0.96,
      "document_hash": "b1cfde40c6ab6b5e9d7f255b3ccec68e4846fb248a0af4feaad062e25c5d717d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b1cfde40c6ab-0001-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Our position has consistently been that the only decisions of the MSPB that can get review in a district court are decisions on the issue of discrimination."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2012-11-184",
      "confidence": 0.93,
      "document_hash": "b1cfde40c6ab6b5e9d7f255b3ccec68e4846fb248a0af4feaad062e25c5d717d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b1cfde40c6ab-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 32,
        "start": 32
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But, Ms. Harrington, go back to the question that the Chief Justice asked you, because the question was: Should we read \"judicially reviewable action\" as something different from action subject to judicial review, which is how you would normally read that language, as something different from just final agency action that you can take to a court."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Harrington",
      "case_id": "2012-11-184",
      "confidence": 0.94,
      "document_hash": "b1cfde40c6ab6b5e9d7f255b3ccec68e4846fb248a0af4feaad062e25c5d717d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b1cfde40c6ab-0001-0005",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the plaintiffs could then file a suit in district court and seek equitable tolling for having missed the deadline to file from the date of the final agency decision."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2012-11-184",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b1cfde40c6ab6b5e9d7f255b3ccec68e4846fb248a0af4feaad062e25c5d717d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b1cfde40c6ab-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, didn't -- in the Ballentine case, didn't the MSPB take the position that it didn't go to the Federal circuit?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Harrington",
      "case_id": "2012-11-184",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b1cfde40c6ab6b5e9d7f255b3ccec68e4846fb248a0af4feaad062e25c5d717d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b1cfde40c6ab-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Our brief is filed on behalf of all the agencies in the United States that are affected by this."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2012-11-184",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b1cfde40c6ab6b5e9d7f255b3ccec68e4846fb248a0af4feaad062e25c5d717d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b1cfde40c6ab-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 43,
        "start": 43
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Ms. Harrington, would you agree that this is a remarkably strange way of Congress trying to accomplish this objective?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Harrington",
      "case_id": "2012-11-184",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b1cfde40c6ab6b5e9d7f255b3ccec68e4846fb248a0af4feaad062e25c5d717d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b1cfde40c6ab-0002-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In our view, you should not read that exception more broadly than necessary to accommodate employees' rights to have their discrimination claims determined de novo in district court."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2012-11-184",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b1cfde40c6ab6b5e9d7f255b3ccec68e4846fb248a0af4feaad062e25c5d717d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b1cfde40c6ab-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "with your opposing counsel's position that once the Board decides the CSRA claim and the discrimination claim, the district court reviews both?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Schnapper",
      "case_id": "2012-11-184",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b1cfde40c6ab6b5e9d7f255b3ccec68e4846fb248a0af4feaad062e25c5d717d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b1cfde40c6ab-0002-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 53,
        "start": 53
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Our answer is all. The Government's answer, the rule that is derived from Ballentine, has confounded the lower courts since Ballentine and those problems are reflected in the divergent accounts of the rule in the Government's brief."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2012-11-184",
      "confidence": 0.0,
